    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5500B\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the disclosure\nof public employee disciplinary records\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide all public employees with notice whenever their personal\ninformation has been released to the public pursuant to a FOIL request.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1 of the bill amends section 87 of the Public Officers Law by\nadding a new subdivision 4-c to effectuate the purposes  of  the  legis-\nlation.\n\n  Section 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDuring  the  2020 Legislative Session, legislation was enacted to repeal\nthe provisions of § 50-a of the Civil Rights Law and to amend § 86,\n  § 87, and § 89 of the Public Officers Law. These cumulative  statutory\nchanges  effectively  removed  privacy  protections  for our State's law\nenforcement officers, and all public employees, by making their  person-\nnel  records  accessible to the public via a simple FOIL request.  While\nseeking to provide the public with greater access to personnel files  of\npolice  officers, corrections officers, firefighters and paramedics, the\nLegislature failed to ensure that these dedicated civil  servants  whose\npersonal  information  is subject to a FOIL request be provided any form\nof notice of such disclosure. This legislation  simply  recognizes  that\nthese  impacted  public  employees should have minimum notice when their\npersonal information has been released to the public.\n\nThis proposed legislation would not affect the  release  of  information\nthat  is  now  permissible following the changes to the Civil Rights Law\nand the Public Officers Law in 2020. Rather, it would simply ensure that\nif a public employee's personal information has  been  released  to  the\npublic, then such affected employee would have notice of such release.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
